{
  "id": "Lyo.Idempotency.Postgres",
  "name": "Lyo.Idempotency.Postgres",
  "area": "Core",
  "tagline": "PostgreSQL idempotency store. Schema idempotency, table entry. API claims and outbox rows share one unique index.",
  "description": "PostgresIdempotencyStore writes kind=api from TryBegin and kind=outbox from InsertOutbox. A caller transaction gets a savepoint around the insert. On 23505 the store rolls back to that savepoint and re-reads the live row. The caller transaction stays open.",
  "features": [
    "**One live row per scope and key.** The unique index is (scope, key) where state is in_progress, completed, or failed. Expired rows stay in the table and are not in the index.",
    "**Outbox insert does not commit.** InsertOutbox uses the caller's DbTransaction. A different payload rolls that transaction back and throws ConflictException."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Register",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "services.AddPostgresIdempotency(new PostgresIdempotencyOptions {\n    ConnectionString = connectionString,\n    EnableAutoMigrations = true\n});"
    }
  ],
